senses.gloss:
अञ्ज् अन॑क्ति अङ्क्ते॑ pp. अक्त॑ smear, anoint, adorn (M.
refl.);
 glorify, extol;
 make clear, manifest. C. अञ्जयति smear,
anoint. — अनु anoint. अभि smear, anoint (M. refl.), adorn. आ
anoint, smooth, embellish, glorify. नि smear, anoint;
 M. slip into,
hide among (अन्तर्). प्रति anoint, adorn. वि M. anoint throughout;
anoint or adorn one's self with (instr. or acc.);
 make clear, bring to
notice, betray. C. cause to become clear, reveal. अभिवि P. become
clear, appear. सम् anoint, adorn, embellish, honour;
 join, unite;
lick, devour;
 M. feed on (instr.). — Cf. अभिव्यक्त, अभ्यक्त,
व्य॑क्त.

अञ्जन n. smearing, anointing;
 suggesting ((rh.));
 ointment,
paint, esp. a collyrium made of antimony.

अ॑ञ्जस् n. ointment;
 instr. & acc. quickly, suddenly (lit. in
a slippery way or with gliding motion).

अञ्जि॑ a. smearing, slippery (also अञ्जिव॑);
 m. n. ointment,
paint, colour, ornament.
